  "final_message": "Task 1 is done and recorded in the ledger: `Task 1: complete (commits 7590d6d..82a54d7, mutants: 9/9, tests: \u2026 \u2192 8 passed)`. It passed on the first `task-done` run.\n\n**New tests.** The plan's two tests only checked age 5 and age 30. They never checked the senior rule or either age cutoff. I added six tests for ages 0, 11, 12, 64, 65 and 80, and they passed against the existing code. They are in a separate commit, `82a54d7`, and the two plan tests are unchanged.\n\n**Mutant run.** I wrote 9 deliberately wrong versions of `tickets.py`, and the tests caught all of them. They cover:\n- the wrong full price;\n- off-by-one errors at the 12 and 65 cutoffs, both in the comparison and in the constants;\n- dropping the child discount or the senior discount;\n- charging full price where the discount applies;\n- leaving age 0 out of the child discount.\n\nEvery test the task added fails on the version of the code from before the task, because `tickets.py` doesn't exist there and the test file can't load.\n\nThe full list of mutants and which test covers which age is in `.sdd/plan/task-1-mutants.md`, and the run log is `.sdd/plan/task-1-mutants.log`.\n\nAs instructed, I stopped here and did not start the final review.",
